 "id": "H-0100",
 "title": "MQI verbs called through a data item: CALL identifier whose VALUE names the MQ verb",
 "category": "mq",
 "issue": 4892,
 "shapes": [
  "MQSA MQSADYN: 01 WS-V-CONN PIC X(8) VALUE 'MQCONN' (likewise MQOPEN, MQPUT, MQCLOSE, MQDISC) and CALL WS-V-CONN USING ... instead of CALL 'MQCONN' USING ..."
 ],
 "asserts": "Each CALL in MQSADYN is a call_sites fact of form identifier (operand the data item, target the verb held in its VALUE clause, resolves_to null), with a call edge from the paragraph that holds it and a gaps entry because no estate member holds the MQ stub. The five verb-name data items are data_items. The key does not fold an identifier CALL into a literal CALL, and does not drop it because the verb is a vendor entry point.",
 "citations": [
  {
   "doc": "IBM Enterprise COBOL for z/OS Language Reference",
   "section": "CALL statement",
   "url": "https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/SS6SG3_6.4.0/lr/ref/rlpscall.html",
   "quote": "identifier-1 must be an alphanumeric, alphabetic, or numeric data item described with USAGE DISPLAY such that its value can be a program-name."
  },
  {
